{"availability":"available","full":"cagscalclabs/lwip-ce","name":"lwip-ce","description":"An IP stack implementation for the TI-84+ CE derived from lwIP code. Implements custom memory management for <60K RAM, assembly optimizations, and a custom lightweight TLS stack engineered for the constraints of the system.","category":"Developer tools","language":"C","stars":27,"forks":4,"created":"2023-11-05T01:41:42Z","updated":"2026-10-09T05:03:38Z","license":null,"branch":"master","homepage":"https://cagscalclabs.github.io/lwip-ce/","topics":["networking","ti-84-plus-ce","tls13"],"demo":"https://cagscalclabs.github.io/lwip-ce/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T08:57:02.328Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T08:57:02.328Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T08:57:02.328Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-07T02:54:50.963Z","stars":27,"forks":4},{"at":"2026-10-09T08:57:02.328Z","stars":27,"forks":4}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["The same workflow that generates the nightly release also runs the CI tests, however running this in this way causes the default GitHub badges to never update. To work around this, we export a badge for each test result to img.shield.io, hence the different aesthetic. You can still audit last run output and results from the actions tab.","SAST uses git diff against upstream lwIP to filter out untouched upstream code and scans only targets unique to this repository. For upstream issues, file an issue with nonGNU.","DAST uses a locally-run hardware-in-the-loop workflow because the current emulator does not support Ethernet devices. A helper program runs on the calculator and exposes the DAST target while a local script attaches to it, performs network probes, advances the calculator-side test state, and writes results to JSON. This workflow then parses the JSON report and updates the test state accordingly."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/cagscalclabs/lwip-ce/blob/master/README.md",